WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.560
This Cannabis <i>Japan</i> is wonderful!

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.610
No, awesome!

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:04.730
No, not that!

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.860
How do I say this?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.440
This is a bread that cannot be described with words.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.700
If I were to still try to do so...

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.870
I’d call it a bread that can change history!

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:18.160
This bread is the ultimate bread
that stands at the apex of all others!

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.460
The champions of the Second Monaco Cup are...

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.210
the Japanese representatives!

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.750
The last round of the finals of the Monaco Cup

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.130
ended with the victory of Azuma Kazuma’s Cannabis <i>Japan</i>!

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:36.900
And so, all of the programs in the Second Monaco Cup have been completed!

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.060
Cheers!

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.110
Well, we went through a lot, but in
the end it’s a happily-ever-after ending.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:55.870
Umm... Why’s Suwabara-san so depressed?

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.200
Could it be that his fear of heights is still...?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.040
You still have a long way to go, don’t you, Tsukino?

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.790
Huh?

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.750
He has fallen in love with a
woman from the enemy side.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.090
With this tournament nearing its end,
they have no choice but to separate.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:10.170
That dumb samurai... is lonely.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.180
Is that what it was?!

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.180
Do not say any more than that.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.970
I am a warrior.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.010
Warriors do not waste time on things like love.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.180
M-Me... Monica doesn’t mean anything to...

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.270
Darling!

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.690
M-Monica...

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.020
Hey Kai, I want to join the party, too!

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.900
Oh, go right ahead.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.400
Don’t be kidding around.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.860
We’re enemies.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.150
What do you want to celebrate with us at our table?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.450
Kawachi...

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.870
Don’t be so strict...

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.540
No, no exceptions.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.040
The enemy is the enemy.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.830
But, if you really want to, then...

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.040
Take that eyesore of a
Suwabara with you, and go away.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.420
Be grateful, the two of you...

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.210
This is a chance for you two to be by yourselves.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:51.920
So, you can do all you...

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.130
Are you an idiot?

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.840
What do you mean enemies?!
Aren’t we all like partners now?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.260
Huh?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.890
Didn’t you know?

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.350
Pantasia has merged with St. Pierre,

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.520
and as of now, Mr. Kirisaki
will be in charge of management.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.230
What was that?!

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:16.240
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.160
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.450
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.960
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:29.080
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.540
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.730
A Letter of Challenge from Kirisaki!!

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.970
The start of a new program, Yakitate!! 9!

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.490
To be honest,

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:21.200
I never thought that Kirisaki had moved so far ahead.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.460
The new president has yet to be announced, but...

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.910
the way things look, it looks like it’ll probably be Yukino.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.260
However, we have the 12 billion yen that we won from the Monaco Cup.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.180
If we use this money as capital to set up a new company...

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.600
That’s true...

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:46.020
But, there’s some things in the world
that can’t be resolved with just logic.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.320
We can’t get over this so easily.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.560
Especially her.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.410
Cheer up.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:58.490
If you aren’t happy,
none of us can be, either.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.520
I’m sorry.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.780
But, I know how hard my
grandfather worked to establish Pantasia.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.130
Th-This is...

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.970
The MVP prize...

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.430
I’ll give you that, so cheer up.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.470
Is that okay?

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.810
Something so precious...?

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.180
It’s all right.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.890
A ring would simply get in my way when I knead bread.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.100
Either way,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.320
you’ve given me this hairband, so this is in returning the favor.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.790
B-But...

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.560
You should accept it.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.320
According to Monaco legend,

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:40.290
if you have that ring, the hero
Pierrot will appear before you.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.980
B-But...

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.750
Yeah, you should accept it, Tsukino.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.460
I don’t know if a hero’s gonna come,

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.990
but it’s a ring that’s supposed to bring good tidings.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.220
Th-That’s true. Well...

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:54.310
B-But... He put it on the ring finger of my left hand...

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:00.250
What do you mean I’m not going to be made Pantasia’s president?

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:07.230
Buying up all those shares, bringing
the board of directors over to our side...

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:10.020
Do you know just how hard I’ve worked for this?!

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.070
Don’t tell me... You’re thinking of betraying me...?

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.430
Listen to what I have to say to the very end.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.120
I’m going to have you be president of St. Pierre.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.040
As a reward for your work,

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.710
I’ve transferred a large percentage of
the St. Pierre stock under your name.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.880
In both name and reality, you’ll be the president representing the company.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.950
Then, what are <i>you</i> going to do?!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.630
There’s one other thing that needs to be done,

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:36.750
so I’ve decided to retire from all official managerial positions.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.510
Well, I guess I’m fine with that.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:43.470
Well then, who’s going to be president of Pantasia?

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.690
The new president of Pantasia is Tsukino?!

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:47.810
Yeah.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:51.190
I just received the official confirmation
from the Pantasia Main Branch.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:52.890
So, that’s how he’s playing it, eh?

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:57.150
After buying the shares and becoming the owner,

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:01.530
all he plans to do is appoint a
president who would bring in the money.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:05.290
Rather than make us, the possessors of wealth in the order of 12 billion, his enemies,

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:08.320
he must have decided that it’s smarter to bring us over to his side.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:12.590
So, I guess that means that he plans
to reel us in as much as possible, huh?

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:13.550
Yeah.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:17.380
Hey Tsukino, you can’t accept this offer!

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:20.390
I know that you have feelings for Pantasia,

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:21.800
but this is a trap!

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:22.720
This is a dangerous trap!

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.420
How regrettable for you to think that this is a trap...

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.270
Ki-Kirisaki!

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.770
Because, what I want to have is a battle.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:30.840
A battle?

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.310
What do you think?

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.280
Would you accept my challenge?

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:38.110
It would be a face-off between St. Pierre and Pantasia.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:44.080
Should you win, I’ll hand over all
of the stock that I own in Pantasia.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:51.960
Should you accept, the battle will be broadcast
all over Japan on the Greater Tokyo TV station.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:56.050
However, the televising and production fees of the program must be paid for

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.300
with the 12 billion yen in your possession.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:03.790
Are you conspiring to have us
self-destruct by using up our 12 billion?

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.560
I won’t deny it.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:09.600
However, I own about 60% of Pantasia’s stock.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.520
It is valued at about 120 billion yen,
and I will be betting it.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.310
If you don’t bear some risk
as well, if won’t be a fair fight.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.570
So, what are the rules of this battle?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:24.370
Without knowledge of the opponents
we’ll fight, or the method of the battle,

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.860
there’s no way we can reply to your challenge.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.000
Oh, sorry about that.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.710
The name of the bread program is Yakitate!! 9.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:35.130
There is no restriction to the number or age of the contestants.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:39.550
But, we’d like for Azuma Kazuma-kun to participate in every match.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.460
That is the request of the people from the TV station.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:42.670
Huh, me?

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:48.560
At the mere age of 16, you
became the MVP at a world tournament.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.430
The media all over the world has
taken notice of your performance.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.140
Kazuma...

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:58.040
Kazuma has become so flat!!!

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.140
This is a newspaper, Grandpa.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.140
And the method of the battle?

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.860
A system of panel-battle.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:09.290
Nine cities with specialty products
will be spread over a 3x3 panel.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:12.150
And what you have to do is wrangle over the squares.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.650
What do you mean by cities with specialty products?

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:17.750
Ever heard of the city of Kitakata?

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.630
Of course I have.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.670
Isn’t it the place famous for its ramen?

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:22.840
Exactly.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:25.830
Now, do you know of a city that’s famous for their bread, rather than their ramen?

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.220
I don’t really think so...

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.180
So, that’s what we’re going to try to create.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:35.480
I believe the reason why bread hasn’t really gained popularity in Japan is that

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:39.690
unlike ramen, there are no breads
that are exclusive to one particular place.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:45.200
Since Azuma-kun is aiming for a <i>Japan</i>,
he would agree with my opinion, right?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.420
The city of Kitakata claims that its water is delicious,

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.620
and rose to fame by using it in their ramen.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.290
A baker of your skill

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:57.700
should be able to create various <i>Japan</i>s that integrate the specialty foods of each city.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.710
I-I...

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:05.720
I just wanted to show my grandpa, who ate nothing but rice, that bread was delicious, too.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.960
That’s why I started attempting to create the <i>Japan</i>.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:10.260
That’s why I’m really happy

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.390
when I can make all kinds of
people eat really delicious bread.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:15.300
But...

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:19.270
I believe that all of us share

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:24.190
the sentiment of wanting all kinds of people to realize the wonder

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.820
of the thing called bread.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.390
Don’t feed us lines!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.900
Please don’t put us on the same level as you.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.900
This <i>Gopan</i> #104 is something I created for fun.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:37.400
<i>Gopan</i> #104?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.380
Here, try it.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.390
There’s red rice, fried rice, and Chinese omelette on rice,

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.350
but America’s rice, <i>Gohan</i>, does not exist.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:00.480
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.960
This story is a cool, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses the North Pole Hands,

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:09.240
Tom Crusoe, who will create an American rice made by and for the American people,

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:13.360
Note: Gohan (<b>ご飯) means “cooked rice.”
The “han” part means “rice,” so... “Go!” han.
<i>Gohan</i>, which can be presented to the world proudly.</b>

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:15.660
He has arrived!!

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.960
The boy who possesses the North Pole Hands!

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.820
This is my special recipe, <i>Gohan</i> #55, the fermented soybean <i>gohan</i>!

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.010
Chichioya!

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.960
What’s with this “chichioya”?! Call me Daddy!

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:32.670
Daddy, how about we have
rice for breakfast once in a while?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.680
No, no, no, no, no. No!

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.270
We are wheat farmers in California!

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.440
What’s this about rice?!

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.420
You dumb Japanese-wannabe!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:45.930
Daddy says that because he hasn’t ever eaten <i>real</i> rice!

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:47.650
Hey, li’l Tom.

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:48.930
Welcome.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:53.190
I tried the idea of rice with Daddy, but he was completely against it.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:57.700
If we could eat rice just like cereal,
then even Daddy would...

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.830
Oh, is that all?

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.190
Huh? You can do that?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:05.130
To begin with, the potential to go with pretty much any type of meal is hidden within rice,

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:08.700
depending on the trick you apply while cooking it.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.300
Li’l Tom...

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.970
You’ll create <i>Gohan</i> for your father.

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:13.710
Me?!

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:15.470
I believe that you can do it.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:19.710
You, who possess the North Pole Hands
that are most suited to washing rice.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:21.390
North Pole Hands?

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.270
I see...

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.230
I thought that I was just sensitive to the cold...

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.720
You can call it <i>Gohan</i> once
people like your father approve of it.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.900
Th-This is...

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.740
Just like the first episode of Yakitate!! Japan...

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:36.620
Wh-What is this white, goopy stuff?!

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.160
It is Japanese-style cereal.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.490
It’s porridge made from unmilled rice and milk, Daddy.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.670
Who could possibly eat something that gross?!

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:47.220
You can complain all you want after at least one bite.

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.720
Just one bite, then.

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:56.330
Jesus!

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:00.840
After eating okayu, I’m off to the hills!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.850
I’m making a promise with the rice,

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.550
and I’m firmly milking the cow.

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:08.190
D-Delicious.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:09.560
This is really good.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:10.810
Yay!

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.620
It’s been ten years since.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:19.880
After creating 55 versions of <i>Gohan</i>, I set off for Japan.

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:21.160
<b>Shiroyanagi</b>

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:24.240
We will now begin the employment
exam for the Gohanya Main Branch.
<b>Shiroyanagi</b>

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:24.250
We will now begin the employment
exam for the Gohanya Main Branch.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.920
I’ll fight you with <i>Gohan</i>!

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:27.840
<b>Kishiwada
What do you mean by <i>Gohan</i>?</b>

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.410
Is this guy gonna be okay?
<b>Kishiwada</b>

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:29.420
<b>Kishiwada</b>

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:29.840
The day the Rocky Mountains fell!
Burnt Black!!

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.420
Next time, on Takitate!! Gohan,

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:32.050
Burnt Black!!

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:33.760
The day the Rocky Mountains fell!

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:34.910
Be sure to watch!

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.620
Takitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:41.640
The history of porridge in Japan dates back to the Yayoi Age.
Note: The Yayoi Age extends from around the 3rd to the 2nd century BC

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.560
If was originally made by boiling unmilled rice.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.630
When steamed, it was called “okowa.”

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.450
Oh?!

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:53.900
H-How can this be?!

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:58.120
With his <i>Japan</i> #61, Azuma was able to
make a bread that could change history,

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:03.910
but this <i>Gopan</i> #104 changed our
Yakitate!! Japan into Takitate!! Gohan,

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:06.110
complete with a preview of the next
episode and the Seed of Knowledge!

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.630
I... I lose.

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:10.050
How was it?

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.210
My <i>Gopan</i> #104...

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.630
While you may have gotten the MVP at the Monaco Cup,

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:19.220
it was ultimately a battle between young bakers under the age of 22.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:20.350
You forget that the world...

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:26.650
no, that even Japan still has many skillful bakers.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.480
Azuma-kun.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:32.140
Don’t you wish to battle it out with such artisans?

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:34.110
I do.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:35.780
I want to fight it out with them.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:36.640
But...

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:40.150
Azuma-san.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:44.370
Well, either way, the new president is still young.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:46.000
I shall await your answer after you return to Japa...

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.150
No.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.650
We will accept your offer right now.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:50.820
Tsukino!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.760
Are you serious, Tsukino-san?

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:57.080
If we lose, we’ll lose everything.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.340
No matter what the dangers might be,

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:03.850
I cannot simply hand over Grandfather’s Pantasia to these people.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:09.020
However, the 12 billion yen that we have now belongs to all of us.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:12.300
Therefore, it is necessary for everyone to feel the same way about this.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:18.490
As the new president, Tsukino-sama, wishes.

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:19.810
Manager!

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.080
Sounds like fun.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.310
I’ll come along with you.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:25.780
I guess it can’t be helped.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.000
Yahoo!

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.370
Then, it’s decided!

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:29.530
Let’s do it!

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.790
Prepare yourself.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.090
I won’t lose next time.

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:36.170
I’ll defeat you with the best <i>Japan</i> ever.

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.340
Then, it’s decided.

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:43.920
The curtain is raised on the final showdown
between Pantasia and St. Pierre!

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.430
We can finally get back to Japan.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:56.930
Yeah...

00:15:57.570 --> 00:16:00.450
It’s good to be looking forward to returning home.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:03.530
However, you will have the trial of fighting it out with the seasoned masters of St. Pierre

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.490
who are waiting for you.

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.290
We can’t just focus on winning.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:11.950
We have to be careful not to do anything to hurt the reputation of Pantasia.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.450
Especially you, Kawachi!

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.550
If you’re going to be on TV,

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:18.790
do not wear those ghastly afro wigs you wore in the past!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.180
Ridiculous!

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.210
What’s so ghastly about an afro?!

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.800
I guess we simply differ in our perception of beauty.

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:30.180
Somebody who displays absurd reactions like you has no sense for beauty, either!

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.900
What part of my reactions are you calling absurd?!

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:38.100
Kuroyanagi-sama, there’s a passenger in first class who’d like to see you.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.440
A passenger in first class?

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.650
Welcome to first class.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.490
Please take the seat next to me.

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.570
I’m fine as I am.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:53.990
I’ll tell you from the start that if you
wish to recruit me, you may as well give up.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.460
Unfortunately, that is not what
I wished to speak to you about.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.750
I wish for you to stop being a baker.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:04.840
What was that?!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:08.380
And, you should become a professional food critic,

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:12.590
the judge and master of ceremonies
for our program, Yakitate!! 9.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.680
I believe that your sensitivity to taste

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:21.350
and great knowledge of various kinds of food items are exceptional.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.360
I don’t think that there can be
anyone as competent as you.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.360
Ridiculous.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:29.860
Even if that were the case,
I just might side with Azuma’s side.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.740
I don’t think so.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.620
Your soul as a judge is first-class.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:39.870
You cannot possibly judge something delicious as bad, nor something bad as delicious.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.960
I’m happy that my ability as a judge is so highly esteemed,

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:50.380
but I have no intentions of throwing
away my life as a baker or food scientist yet.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.640
There’s no need to rush your decision, Kuroyanagi-kun.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:54.710
Sorry for the wait.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:59.220
The only reason I offered this to you
is because I think that it’s a shame

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.980
to see your talent going to waste.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.560
Kuroyanagi-kun...

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.520
If you were to become the judge of Yakitate!! 9,

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.230
you could put that talent of
yours to use to your heart’s desire.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:14.240
You can be successful in life only if you are not greedy, and choose a single path to walk down.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.740
Take your time and think over it carefully.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.290
Hey, Manager...

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:19.790
I’ve been thinking about this for a while.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:23.330
Why are you on such bad terms with Old Man Kuroyanagi?

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.960
Wasn’t Old Man Kuroyanagi
your apprentice in the past?

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:30.210
Yeah, I’ve been wanting to ask you that for a while myself.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.720
This sounds interesting.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.960
Yeah, it’s annoying. Just say it.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:35.890
Manager...?

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.560
It guess it can’t be helped, then.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:43.970
When he became my apprentice,
I harassed him all the time.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:48.230
Then, you mean it’s all <i>your</i> fault?

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.400
That’s right.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.820
But...

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:54.150
This is what happened on the
first day of his apprenticeship.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.650
What wonderful French bread.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.540
252.4 grams of hatsuga genmai yeast,

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:03.330
851.5 grams of French flour,

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:08.000
21.1 grams of salt, and 5.2 grams of malt.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:12.050
The fermentation time is 238 minutes and 40 seconds.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:15.510
It was baked at 300 degrees
for 4 minutes and 45 seconds,

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:18.420
and at 250 degrees for 25 minutes and 20 seconds...

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:21.080
All of the conditions of the French bread

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:24.180
are set to best complement today’s temperature and humidity.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.850
Even the fermentation and baking times are perfect...

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.150
Matsushiro-san is truly a genius!

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:32.360
I couldn’t believe what I was hearing then.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:36.150
With only his sense of taste, sight and smell,

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:41.160
he figured it out perfectly, down to the tenth of a gram, and to the second needed for baking.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:42.330
That’s amazing!

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.120
Just as you’d expect of Kuroyanagi-senpai!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.500
It’s unbelievable...

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.080
He isn’t human.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:51.290
Then, why did you harass him, Manager?

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:57.050
From the very first day of his apprenticeship
with me, I no longer wanted him to be a baker.

00:19:57.050 --> 00:20:00.550
I believed that he should
become a professional food critic.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.390
At first, I thought to convince him of that immediately.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:08.060
But, he’s really straightforward,
stubborn and surprisingly hardworking.

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:12.400
So, I didn’t think that he would
listen to the opinion of a stranger

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.320
who was just looking at his work every few days.

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:17.780
So, you felt you had no choice but to harass him.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:23.790
But, I think that Kuro-yan would probably
want to tell you to mind your own business.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:26.030
Exactly, Kawachi. Well said.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.080
I think you know this, too.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:33.290
In any field, only a handful of people can be at the top.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:39.300
Having noticed someone who could
stand at the top, I couldn’t just ignore it.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.050
Also, he’s special.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:46.690
After all, he’s my... first apprentice.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:56.150
This is the opinion of me, your second apprentice...

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.900
Who is my second apprentice?!

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.160
I’ve never thought of you as my apprentice!

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.650
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:05.620
If you still feel that way,
Manager, you can still make it happen.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.660
You just have to put it into words
and tell him honestly what you feel.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.730
You’re so shy.

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:10.710
Not possible.

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.750
He’s just stupid for not having figured it out from my attitude toward him.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.750
You were lucky enough to be born a human,
so why not use words to tell him?

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:18.790
Or are you a Neanderthal?

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.380
Who you calling a Neanderthal?!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:25.850
My one and only master is a Neanderthal, eh?

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.680
Ah! Neanderthals are so violent!

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:28.820
I didn’t learn much about baking from you, but...
Ah! Neanderthals are so violent!

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.140
I didn’t learn much about baking from you, but...

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.100
Sir!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.450
I learned which path I must take.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.530
Greater Tokyo TV
A few weeks later

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:48.410
It’s been about 400 years
since the Battle of Sekigahara.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:51.830
Now marks the beginning of another great showdown that will split apart the heavens.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:55.380
And, this battle is called... Yakitate!! 9!

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:58.840
The judge and master of ceremonies is... me,

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:00.970
Kuroyanagi Ryou!

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:06.260
The Super Taste Judge, Kuroyanagi Ryou!

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.050
Engrave that name into your ears!

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:10.480
That’s right.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:13.650
At last, it’s time for the final showdown between St. Pierre and Pantasia.

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:15.560
Yakitate!! 9!

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:18.310
Here are the contestants!

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.440
Starting with the Pantasia representatives...

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:21.570
Azuma Kazuma.

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:22.780
Kanmuri Shigeru.

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:24.320
Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:26.780
And their opponent,
the St. Pierre representative...

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.910
A member of CMAP, Tsubodzuka Takumi!

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.100
Our first opponent is a pop idol!

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:09.600
Just as you’d expect of Greater Tokyo TV.

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:11.220
That’s some good casting.

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:12.640
Don’t let down your guard.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:14.770
He’s no ordinary pop idol.

00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:16.350
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:17.480
The bread battle in special localities!!

00:24:17.480 --> 00:24:18.860
In the end, he’s a pop idol!

00:24:18.860 --> 00:24:19.860
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:22.610
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:24.570
Takitate!! Gohan!

00:24:24.570 --> 00:24:24.850
You should not eat rice immediately after cooking it.

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:26.860
Don’t eat immediately after cooking

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:27.860
If you eat it after steaming it further for about 15 minutes,

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:29.240
Eat after steaming for about 15 more minutes

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:30.590
it’ll become soft and sticky!
Eat after steaming for about 15 more minutes

00:24:30.590 --> 00:24:31.630
it’ll become soft and sticky!

00:24:32.120 --> 00:24:34.340
I know that...
